WEBVTT

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.680
<i>Suzumegahara faces Mozuyama Junior High,
a team that reached Nationals,</i>

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.690
<i>in a practice match.</i>

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:14.960
<i>Hanabi lost, and then 
Hokuto was defeated, too.</i>

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.950
<i>But Munemune and Kiruka fired back
with a doubles win,</i>

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.780
<i>bringing us to the fourth match,</i>

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:25.210
<i>in which Agari will take on
Mozuyama's captain, Zashikiwarashi Zakuro.</i>

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.210
<i>Their fiery battle is about to begin!</i>

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:32.300
Now, then.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.410
We may have lost in doubles,

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:36.680
but we still hold a 2-1 lead.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:38.800
With Captain Zakuro up next,

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.060
this match is ours!

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:49.860
Why do you play
the life-or-death game of table tennis?

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:56.450
Jeez, what's gotten into you?

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:58.070
You've been spacing out all day!

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:00.280
Ow! Id hurdz!

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:03.070
Come on, pull yourself together.

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:06.120
Or else...

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.760
...you'll miss out
on the most heart-racing moment.

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:14.450
<i>Heart-racing moment?</i>

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:18.880
<i>The reason I play table tennis...</i>

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:21.430
First game.

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:22.970
Kamiya to serve.

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:24.910
<i>The reason...</i>

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:27.190
Love-all!

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:59.180
<b>Scorching</b>

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:59.180
<b>Ping Pong Girls</b>

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:39.890
...you'll miss out
on the most heart-racing moment.

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:41.100
Oh? You went to Karasuma?

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.720
We seniors will see just how good you are.

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.520
I love the way you play
table tennis, Futamaru-san!

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:15.790
<b>Ninth Serve</b>

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:15.790
<b>Never Reach Me</b>

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:28.180
<i>There!</i>

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:35.150
<i>Again?</i>

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:37.110
Six-all.

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:44.120
N-No wonder she's captain of Mozuyama,
a national-caliber team.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:46.330
She keeps catching up
to Agari-senpai immediately.

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.350
I don't know if I'd call it "catching up."

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:51.200
Yeah, it's more like
Agari can't build any sort of lead.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.000
Even though she's going all guns blazing.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:57.770
Mozuyama's captain is a klutz,
but she's pretty tenacious.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.210
Agari-chan...

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:03.340
Eight-all.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:05.350
<i>Not again!</i>

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:07.720
<i>She returns the ball,
no matter where I hit it!</i>

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:15.400
<i>Again and again, like it's only natural.</i>

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:26.240
Why don't you take a seat, Kururi-senpai?

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:28.260
Zakuro's playing,

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:30.750
so I'll stay on my feet and cheer her on.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:32.540
R-Right.

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:35.960
<i>Fight to the death, Zakuro.</i>

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:39.170
Thirteen-all.

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:41.340
<i>I'm...</i>

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:44.300
Fourteen-thirteen!

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:47.980
Fifteen-thirteen!

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:49.310
Game to Zakuro!

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:50.670
No! Agari!

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:51.890
White Panties.

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:54.770
She caught up, and then overtook me!

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:02.960
<i>That's right. I'm here for you.</i>

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:15.890
2 Years Ago

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:09.570
I'm Futamaru Kururi.

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:13.940
I went to Karasuma Table Tennis Academy
during grade school.

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:15.890
Pleased to meet you.

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:17.580
Karasuma Table Tennis Academy?

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:20.040
You went to that super-famous
table tennis club?

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:20.720
Wow!

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.130
You must be really good!

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:25.590
Oh? You went to Karasuma?

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:30.700
Though I hear all sorts go there.

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:33.060
You can't be anything special
if you came to our school.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:36.980
A lot of people use brand names like that
to make themselves look better.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:38.300
This is perfect.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:43.280
As part of the newcomer orientation,
we seniors will see just how good you are.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:46.640
<i>I'd been playing table 
tennis since I was little,</i>

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:47.750
<i>so as soon as I joined,</i>

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:51.700
<i>I became the center of attention 
among the seniors and those my age.</i>

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:52.590
Sure.

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:57.460
<i>I responded in kind
and took on all comers...</i>

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:00.420
<i>beating them all to death.</i>

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:03.000
The seniors were wiped out.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:05.850
Even the captain was no match for her.

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:10.140
Forget beating Futamaru-san,
none of them even scored a point!

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:11.640
Who...

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:15.600
Who should I play next?

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:22.060
Leaving Notice

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:22.060
I hear the seniors all quit.

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:23.830
Well, they did get destroyed.

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:26.490
She's good, but I think
she took it a bit too far.

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:30.610
There's no place for the weak!

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:34.490
It just goes to show that
the seniors weren't up to scratch.

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:36.510
Hey, Futamaru-san.

00:06:36.510 --> 00:06:40.430
Let's take this chance
to create a legend this year.

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:41.530
Legend?

00:06:41.530 --> 00:06:43.250
Yeah, Nationals.

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:44.500
We shoot for Nationals.

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:47.000
We're a mediocre, no-name school, right?

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:51.410
If a team like ours suddenly made it
to Nationals, we'd be overnight stars!

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:52.950
Nationals? Awesome!

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:53.960
That sounds good.

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:55.150
Let's do it.

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:58.000
So, yeah, you're the captain starting today.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:06:59.420
Teach us all you know.

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:01.190
Make us better players.

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:02.230
Thanks in advance.

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:06.110
<i>After being hailed as a prodigy
as soon as I joined,</i>

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:09.420
<i>I was begged to make the team stronger.</i>

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:10.980
Sure.

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:14.950
<i>I responded in kind and trained them all,</i>

00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:17.680
<i>working them to death.</i>

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:19.910
If you want to get better at table tennis,

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:23.040
hit, hit, and hit some more.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:25.880
Victory will be decided
by who has played more.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:28.440
S-Say, isn't this too much?

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:31.440
Maybe think about changing the workload?

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:32.340
I-I mean, look.

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:34.850
Zakuro-san's dead again.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:39.330
But if we don't practice a lot,
we won't get better.

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:41.660
We won't get anywhere close to Nationals.

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:43.170
W-Well, yeah...

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:44.520
Very well.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:48.070
Shall we move on to serious practice, then?

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:52.990
I'm doubling the workload
starting next month.

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:54.260
Keep that in mind.

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:06.560
<i>Why?</i>

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:11.130
Leaving Notice

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:11.130
<i>I just played them normally.</i>

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:15.300
We've lost all face
now that a junior defeated us.

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:19.850
<i>I just trained them hard
to help them get better.</i>

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:24.730
I only wanted to go to Nationals
'cause it sounded like fun.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:31.570
Leaving Notice

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:28.670
I want no part of practice
if it's going to be this hard.

00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:31.570
Sorry, Futamaru-san.
You're too different.

00:08:32.170 --> 00:08:35.280
<i>All I did was do as they asked.</i>

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:36.480
I'm sorry.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:39.740
Leaving Notice

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:37.620
Sorry.

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:38.520
Goodbye.

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:39.740
Good luck.

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:45.960
<i>Why does everyone leave me?</i>

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:51.600
<i>Was I mistaken?</i>

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:56.140
Morning!

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:06.990
All right!

00:09:06.990 --> 00:09:08.230
Zakuro-senpai!

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:10.770
That's the way, Captain Zakuro!

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:12.480
One-all!

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:18.420
You're awesome!

00:09:21.350 --> 00:09:23.430
Zakuro-san?

00:09:23.910 --> 00:09:26.140
Wh-Why did you come?

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:30.660
What? Didn't you say we'd be adding
morning practices this month?

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:33.470
That's why I pushed myself to wake up early.

00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:35.490
I thought you would've quit.

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:37.050
I-I won't quit!

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:39.750
<i>This girl, who's always the first to drop...</i>

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:43.520
<i>This awkward, clumsy, and klutzy girl...</i>

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:48.210
Sure, practice is hard,
and you're a bit scary,

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:52.730
but I love the way you play
table tennis, Futamaru-san!

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:59.540
After I saw you play the seniors
back when we joined the team,

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:02.450
I decided I wanted to be as good as you,

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:04.700
to play awesome table tennis like you!

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:10.880
So I won't give up,
no matter how hard practice is.

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:11.630
Wait...

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:13.620
Whoa! Are you crying?!

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:15.020
What? Why?!

00:10:15.020 --> 00:10:18.500
I-I-I'm not! My eyes are just drooling!

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:20.020
What the heck? Gross!

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:23.060
<i>I...</i>

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:28.020
<i>I...</i>

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:33.360
<i>I was right!</i>

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:44.030
<i>I must get better!</i>

00:10:51.530 --> 00:10:54.840
<i>A lot better, and then
a lot better than that!</i>

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:05.430
<i>In order to remain Zakuro's ideal player,</i>

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:07.310
<i>I'll push myself to be the best!</i>

00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:24.570
Wow! I want to play like that, too!

00:11:24.570 --> 00:11:25.670
I don't think that's happening.

00:11:25.670 --> 00:11:26.700
Not happening.

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:27.510
Mod habbeninf!

00:11:27.510 --> 00:11:31.000
Wh-Why do you all have to
rain on my parade?!

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:35.280
<i>I can't score!</i>

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:43.550
<i>My forehand smash...</i>

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:52.230
<i>...isn't working!</i>

00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:00.110
Thirteen-twelve.

00:12:06.430 --> 00:12:09.790
...you'll miss out
on the most heart-racing moment.

00:12:13.510 --> 00:12:14.830
Fourteen-twelve.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:16.290
Game to Zakuro.

00:12:16.290 --> 00:12:17.430
All right!

00:12:17.430 --> 00:12:20.270
Way to go, Zakuro-senpai!

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:22.660
Zakuro-senpai!

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:25.880
Don't give up, Agari!

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:24.800
Agari-chan...

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:29.010
You're awesome, Captain!

00:12:44.010 --> 00:12:47.370
Who knew your forehand smashes
could get nullified?

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:53.040
Agari-chan—

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:55.500
Please begin the fourth game.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:56.620
Later.

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:17.370
<i>What tenacity! What willpower!</i>

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:20.720
<i>That's the captain
who led Mozuyama to Nationals for you.</i>

00:13:23.550 --> 00:13:24.650
Seven-eight.

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:27.070
Agari-senpai's fallen behind again!

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:31.540
<i>My forehand can't beat Zakuro-san!</i>

00:13:32.220 --> 00:13:34.570
<i>I can't... I can't!</i>

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:36.060
<i>I can't win!</i>

00:13:38.810 --> 00:13:41.340
<i>My forehand won't...</i>

00:14:03.510 --> 00:14:05.490
<i>Don't give in, Agari-chan!</i>

00:14:06.170 --> 00:14:07.450
<i>I don't want to lose!</i>

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:09.360
<i>If I lose, Koyori won't get to play!</i>

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:13.160
<i>If I lose, Koyori's heart won't race!</i>

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:16.330
<i>Besides, I...</i>

00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:18.500
<i>I want...</i>

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:22.000
She went from forehand...

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:23.340
...to backhand?

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:24.750
Agari-chan!

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:29.720
<i>I want to win and feel my heart race, too!</i>

00:14:31.860 --> 00:14:33.050
A backhand smash?!

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:35.890
Eight-all!

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:39.070
Agari-senpai brought out her backhand smash!

00:14:39.070 --> 00:14:41.060
It's been a while,
but it's as awesome as ever!

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:57.620
Agari-chan.

00:15:04.710 --> 00:15:06.130
Agari-chan...

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:12.810
Yes! Game point!

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:13.350
She's got this!

00:15:13.780 --> 00:15:17.350
<i>I was targeting her backhand
to nullify her forehand smash!</i>

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:20.450
<i>I can't believe she had
such a lethal backhand smash!</i>

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:24.080
<i>Was she hiding it
until the last possible moment?</i>

00:15:26.290 --> 00:15:27.190
<i>Agari-chan!</i>

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:29.440
<i>Crap!</i>

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:33.080
Eleven-eight.

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:34.700
Game to Kamiya.

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:40.640
You're amazing, Agari-senpai!

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:47.800
Hang in there, Captain!

00:15:48.180 --> 00:15:51.010
Final game. Kamiya to serve.

00:15:51.370 --> 00:15:53.340
<i>The loop drive to smash one-two punch,</i>

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:56.610
<i>the power of her forehand,
the surgical precision of her backhand...</i>

00:15:57.130 --> 00:15:59.470
<i>This girl is really, really good!</i>

00:15:59.800 --> 00:16:00.930
Love-all.

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:05.490
<i>But I have to win!</i>

00:16:05.490 --> 00:16:08.360
<i>If I do, we win the whole match!</i>

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:14.080
<i>As captain of the Mozuyama Table
Tennis Team, I have to win for everyone.</i>

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:17.490
<i>Most of all, I have to win for Kururi!</i>

00:16:26.270 --> 00:16:27.200
Captain...

00:16:28.560 --> 00:16:30.590
Hang in there, Captain Zakuro!

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:32.110
<i>Zakuro...</i>

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:38.010
<i>You're free to play table tennis
any way you see fit.</i>

00:16:42.010 --> 00:16:44.980
This is a present.

00:16:45.340 --> 00:16:47.020
Wow, thank you!

00:16:48.140 --> 00:16:50.610
<i>It's this week's friendship fee.</i>

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:53.110
Now that some
spirited first-years have joined,

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:55.750
the team should get
a lot livelier in our second year!

00:16:57.030 --> 00:16:57.740
Zakuro.

00:16:58.860 --> 00:16:59.910
What is it?

00:17:00.640 --> 00:17:04.720
From now on, you be the captain.

00:17:07.030 --> 00:17:09.550
<i>I'm just doing this for myself.</i>

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:15.550
<i>I'll make Zakuro stand atop the summit
of Nationals as Mozuyama's captain.</i>

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:19.390
<i>That's my dream.</i>

00:17:19.860 --> 00:17:25.390
<i>It's the least I can do to repay you
for being my pillar of support.</i>

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:29.100
She switched?!

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:31.440
She's starting to mix
forehands and backhands!

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:35.530
Eight-all!

00:17:38.630 --> 00:17:39.700
Nine-eight!

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:42.570
Agari-chan!

00:17:52.520 --> 00:17:53.690
Eleven-eight!

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:55.760
Game and match to Kamiya!

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:03.030
Awesome, Agari-senpai!

00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:04.250
You're the best!

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:05.810
Well, Koyori?
Is your heart racing?!

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:10.450
Yeah... Yeah!

00:18:10.450 --> 00:18:11.770
You're amazing, Agari-chan!

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:19.920
<i>I see. That's just it.</i>

00:18:20.470 --> 00:18:23.890
<i>I play table tennis for only one reason.</i>

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:31.040
<i>Until I...</i>

00:18:32.560 --> 00:18:33.820
Sorry, girls.

00:18:34.410 --> 00:18:35.610
I lost.

00:18:36.180 --> 00:18:37.770
Don't worry about it, Captain.

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:39.120
That was a great match.

00:18:39.120 --> 00:18:40.280
It was inspiring.

00:18:40.280 --> 00:18:41.550
Nom! Nom!

00:18:45.440 --> 00:18:46.640
<i>Until I...</i>

00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:48.900
It's all right.

00:18:49.880 --> 00:18:52.680
<i>Until I make my dream come true,</i>

00:18:52.680 --> 00:18:57.690
<i>I will never lose, no matter
what kind of match or who I'm up against.</i>

00:18:58.480 --> 00:18:59.500
Kururi?

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:03.670
I'm going to win, I promise.

00:19:06.190 --> 00:19:08.310
Great game, Agari-chan!

00:19:08.310 --> 00:19:10.540
It was a heated battle that went all the way.

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:12.550
That's Agari for you.

00:19:12.550 --> 00:19:15.400
Beating Mozuyama's captain
is an amazing feat.

00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:16.380
I'm moved.

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:26.350
Suzumegahara          Mozuyama

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:26.350
Tenka Hanabi             Sasorida Sachiko

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:26.350
Itsumo Hokuto            Yuragi Yura

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:26.350
Ushirode Kiruka
Munemune

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:26.350
Kanenashi Mayuu
Hamu Kimiko

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:26.350
Kamiya Agari             Zashikiwarashi Zakuro

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:26.350
Tsumujikaze Koyori           Futamaru Kururi

00:19:24.810 --> 00:19:26.350
Now we're all even.

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:29.350
The next match decides it all.

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:31.950
You're up against the Driver of the East.

00:19:31.950 --> 00:19:33.600
Do your best, Koyori-chan.

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:34.560
G-Got it!

00:19:35.600 --> 00:19:38.190
The rest is in your hands, Koyori.

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:40.450
Yeah!

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:44.950
We will now start the fifth match.

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:47.910
Please check each other's rackets.

00:19:51.820 --> 00:19:54.450
Uh, about your question earlier.

00:19:55.600 --> 00:19:57.750
You asked me why I play table tennis.

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:02.670
I...

00:20:03.790 --> 00:20:06.720
I play because I want
to feel my heart race with you!

00:20:08.960 --> 00:20:12.110
Y-You see, I love table tennis.

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:16.160
So I don't want to enjoy it by myself.

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:20.340
It'd make me really happy if I could
let my opponent feel that ecstasy, too.

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:24.450
That's my answer to your question.

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:32.270
Is that so?

00:20:32.800 --> 00:20:35.880
Well, I'd sure love to see you try.

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:39.090
Anyone and everyone who comes at us...

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:43.550
I will simply beat them to death!

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:49.240
Tsumujikaze versus Futamaru.

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:50.470
Best of five games.

00:20:52.930 --> 00:20:54.440
Love-all!

00:20:57.950 --> 00:20:58.940
<i>It begins.</i>

00:20:59.630 --> 00:21:00.440
<i>The fateful...</i>

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:02.190
<i>...decider!</i>

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:07.910
<i>There's no way
my heart will race with yours.</i>

00:21:09.300 --> 00:21:11.440
<i>Everything I do, I do for Zakuro.</i>

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:16.040
<i>I simply fight for Zakuro</i>

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:20.960
<i>and win for Zakuro!</i>

00:21:25.790 --> 00:21:27.590
<i>It curved sharply toward the forehand?</i>

00:21:33.700 --> 00:21:35.980
She turned her back?
The point's not over yet!

00:21:47.070 --> 00:21:48.110
One-love.

00:21:50.230 --> 00:21:52.080
What the hell was that?

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:54.340
It curved off her racket?

00:21:54.340 --> 00:21:55.810
It totally curved, didn't it?

00:21:55.810 --> 00:21:57.290
What the...

00:21:59.140 --> 00:22:00.920
Too bad.

00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:06.520
Your heart-racing ecstasy

00:22:07.680 --> 00:22:10.890
will never reach me.

00:23:43.860 --> 00:24:00.000
Preview

00:23:45.090 --> 00:23:47.300
There's no way to beat someone like this!

00:23:47.300 --> 00:23:48.610
Koyori-senpai!

00:23:48.610 --> 00:23:50.600
Did I do something to Agari-chan?

00:23:50.600 --> 00:23:52.530
We looked for heart-racing moments together.

00:23:52.530 --> 00:23:54.070
We should be able to feel even better.

00:23:54.070 --> 00:23:54.510
Here it is...

00:23:54.510 --> 00:23:56.080
It feels <i>so</i> good!

00:23:56.080 --> 00:23:57.790
Thanks, Agari-chan.
